RETIRE section retained; markers verified gone; row counts: pre-merge heads 147 + theirs 41 => merged 337 rows)\nsrc/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj\nsrc/clj/yang/io.clj\nsrc/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/claims.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/siteset_publication.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_admission.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_transport.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc\nsrc/cljd/yang/antlr/cst.cljd\nsrc/cljs/yang/antlr/cst.cljs\nsrc/cljs/yang/io.cljs\nsrc/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt\ntest/yang/cc4_budget_runner.clj\ntest/yang/cc4_corpus.clj\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_literal_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj\ncommit d60038efdf536f6379affaad5e4d8879b74bda71\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 02:51:49 2026 +0700\n\n    feat(yang.clojure): port phase 2 — the continuation lane (consumer wiring)\n    \n    Retire the slice-5 outcome model and wire the clj continuation family\n    (clj/try, clj/throw, clj/raise) that Phase 1 landed in the prelude:\n    \n    - lower-tail: throw -> clj/throw, try -> clj/try / clj/try-finally (finally\n      now expressible, one-catch lifted), plain tail values, no outcome tuple.\n      The clj/try thunks are compiler-internal raw lambdas (dsg__raw-fn), never\n      the convention's published descriptor, so clj/try can apply them.\n    - call-entry: installs the clj/try bridge before argument binding; an\n      escaping raise or binding failure delivers {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n      :yang.call/value v} to the caller's raise exit exactly once. The intra-unit\n      private tail lane (token packet) is preserved.\n    - compile-guest-call: the raise exit is clj/raise over the handler stack\n      (a :thrown condition delivers its payload; any other value delivers whole),\n      replacing the u/capture public-bridge.\n    - Retire the wrapper/witness/retention machinery (cell/retained?,\n      dsg__condition_wrapper, dsg__visible_of, dsg__condition_retained,\n      condition->outcome, strip-top-outcome, bind-outcome, the failing? pass,\n      the :adapters outcome routing). The caught value IS the payload.\n    - compile-program boundary answers [:yin.k/ok value]/[:yin.k/error raised]\n      via a top-level clj/try; the clj family is emitted inline (the linked\n      runtime binds the same family from the prelude).\n    - Guest library collection predicates rewrite onto the data/* and kind/*\n      host predicates (coll?/set? added to the kind module), retiring the\n      yin.k/outcome-of + portable adapters.\n    \n    R5 holds: a guest-thrown condition-shaped map is data; only the raise exit\n    delivers conditions. The 38F/13E cell/retained? red is gone; the retention\n    probes and the outcome-model pins are re-expressed or retired with the seam.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | 980 ++++++++++++++-------------------------------\n test/yang/clojure_test.clj | 188 ++++-----\n 2 files changed, 375 insertions(+), 793 deletions(-)\nREADME.md\ndarkstar-cc4-classpath.log\ndarkstar-cc4-fidelity.log\ndarkstar-cc4-post-B.log\ndarkstar-cc4-post-S.log\ndarkstar-cc4-post7-B.log\ndarkstar-cc4-post7-S.log\ndarkstar-cc4-pre-classpath.log\ndarkstar-cc4-pre-members.log\ndarkstar-cc4-pre7-B.log\ndarkstar-cc4-pre7-S.log\njupiter-cc4-